Following our recent Dev Talk introducing some of the many different features coming in the Paths to Glory update, it’s time to take a look at the core feature of Albion’s next update: the Albion Journal. Game Director Robin Henkys sat down to reveal what you can find within its pages when the update launches on July 22.

[previewyoutube=6CJifOQyu6c;full][/previewyoutube]
What is the Albion Journal?	The Albion Journal is an achievement system designed to challenge players to explore Albion’s many gameplay areas.	For new players, this acts as a guide with incentives to explore the various activities available in the game	Veterans, meanwhile, are encouraged to complete the most difficult achievements for truly exclusive rewardsHow does it work?	New players will gain access to the Journal once they've completed the tutorial	Existing characters will have the Journal unlocked when the update arrives	It can be opened directly from the HUD, to view open and completed missions	A mission tracker in the HUD shows your current progress in selected missions	The missions in the journal are sorted into categories, and each category is further split into subcategories
//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/0e4c6f0312f8ba6235136dab0ca22fae00a8beb1.png
Progressing through the Journal	Initial missions in each subcategory are a simple introduction to an area of gameplay	As you progress through a subcategory, missions become increasingly difficult	Missions can be completed out of order, even if they have not yet been unlocked – so don't worry about doing something you don't have a mission for, it will still count
//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/2c5505a6c10e2ae80624ed9bcc9057edd0ad706a.png
Individual Mission Rewards	Each mission grants a reward which can be claimed directly from the Journal UI	These rewards include Silver, Tomes of Insight, Dungeon Maps, and more	Tomes of Learning – a new, non-tradable item – are also available as a reward			These grant Learning Points when used			More difficult missions offer more valuable rewards
//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/b3f79b45fa0f65c6c578d5734d10fda7258008c9.png
Category Rewards	Completing a certain percentage of missions within each main category unlocks unique rewards	Each category has a themed Avatar, Avatar Ring, Wardrobe Item with a Vanity Spell, and Mount Skin	Completing all missions in a category will grant you a super-rare, elite version of the wardrobe item
//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/8fc7d72696ed390b02da17ffda8899cfa91ab131.png
Main Categories
The Journal will launch with five categories:

PvE:
	This category challenges you to participate in Albion’s various PvE activities	The Avatar and Avatar Ring show off your prowess in dungeon exploration	The unique wardrobe item is a six-sided die that you can actually roll	The elite version is a twenty-sided die with a critical-hit celebratory roll animation	The mount skin is a themed Direbear
//assets.albiononline.com/uploads/media/default/media/49b82fcf50aac7fdf88acc55ba46358934943627.png

Gathering:
	Includes gathering and fishing missions	The Avatar and Avatar Ring showcase your key role in Albion’s industry	The wardrobe item is a powered chopping axe with a tree-chopping vanity spell	The elite version features awesome visual effects	The mount skin is a mechanical boar with an integrated barbecue
